    {
      "id": "p0115-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Even after deciding to keep Papyrus' name as-is, the team faced a new issue: \"papyrus\" is a foreign word to begin with, so how should Papyrus' Japanese name be pronounced? Should it follow the English pronunciation or the Japanese pronunciation (roughly \"pah pee roos\")? The team chose the latter.",
        "raw": "Even after deciding to keep Papyrus' name as-is, the team faced a new issue:\n\"papyrus\" is a foreign word to begin with, so how should Papyrus' Japanese\nname be pronounced? Should it follow the English pronunciation or the\nJapanese pronunciation (roughly \"pah pee roos\")? The team chose the latter.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08502084,
          0.37079286,
          0.68215157,
          0.43735714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08297461,
          0.37007857,
          0.70662448,
          0.43842857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          24,
          25,
          26,
          27
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "即使决定保留 Papyrus 的名字，团队仍遇到了一个新问题：“papyrus”（纸莎草）本来就是外来词，那么日语中这个名字该怎么念？是遵循英语发音，还是采用日语发音（大致是“pah pee roos”）？团队选择了后者。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
